# Copy to .env (git-ignored) and fill in. Never commit the real file.
# Read automatically by `python -m pipeline.collect` via pipeline/env.py; a variable already
# exported in your shell always wins over this file. Only the names loaded are ever logged.

# --- required for live collection only ---------------------------------------------------
# Register free at https://data.bus-data.dft.gov.uk/account/signup/ and copy the key from
# Account Settings. The archive replay and the website need no key.
BODS_API_KEY=

# --- optional: timetable versions to preserve alongside position captures -----------------
# One or more official dataset download URLs, separated by commas. These need no API key.
#
# Find them at https://data.bus-data.dft.gov.uk/timetable/?q=Manchester — open a data set and
# use https://data.bus-data.dft.gov.uk/timetable/dataset/<ID>/download/
#
# The two below are Transport for Greater Manchester datasets for the operators that dominate
# our selected area (BNML and BNSM). Do NOT use
# https://data.bus-data.dft.gov.uk/timetable/download/bulk_archive — it is the whole national
# archive at about 1.7 GB and the collector skips anything over 40 MB.
#
# Holding a timetable is not evidence that any journey in the position feed matches it.
BODS_TIMETABLE_URL=https://data.bus-data.dft.gov.uk/timetable/dataset/17472/download/,https://data.bus-data.dft.gov.uk/timetable/dataset/14928/download/

# The photographic view from above (docs/PHOTO_3D_RESEARCH.md): a Google Maps Platform browser key
# restricted to this site's address and the Map Tiles API (written into config.json, which is
# what a browser key is for; never committed), or any https 3D Tiles tileset for a check of the
# viewer, labelled as a sample. Neither set: the view is not offered.
# LM_PHOTO3D_GOOGLE_KEY=
# LM_PHOTO3D_TILESET=
